.Dd November 2, 2026
.Dt WPA_SUPPLICANT.CONF 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm wpa_supplicant.conf
.Nd the networks and settings of wpa_supplicant
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Xr wpa_supplicant 8
reads the file that its
.Fl c
names.
Each line is a
.Ar variable Ns = Ns Ar value
setting, and a line that begins with
.Ql #
is a comment.
Global settings come first; then each network is a block,
.Ql network={ ,
of settings one to a line, closed by
.Ql } .
A string value is given in double quotes; a value without them is a
number, a list of words separated by spaces, or for
.Cm ssid
and
.Cm psk ,
hexadecimal.
.Pp
wpa_supplicant chooses among the networks it finds in a scan by
.Cm priority ,
then by security and signal.
.Ss Global settings
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm ctrl_interface Ns = Ns Ar dir
Open a control interface for
.Xr wpa_cli 8
in
.Ar dir ,
usually
.Pa /var/run/wpa_supplicant .
.It Cm update_config Ns =1
Let
.Cm save_config
rewrite the file.
.It Cm country Ns = Ns Ar CC
The two-letter country code that sets the regulatory domain.
.It Cm pmf Ns = Ns Ar n
Management-frame protection for networks that do not set
.Cm ieee80211w :
0 none, 1 when the access point offers it, 2 required.
.It Cm sae_pwe Ns = Ns Ar n
How SAE derives its password element: 0 by hunting and pecking, 1 by
hashing to the element alone, 2 either.
.El
.Ss Network settings
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm ssid Ns = Ns Qq Ar name
The network's name.
.It Cm scan_ssid Ns =1
Scan for the name directly, for a network that hides it.
.It Cm bssid Ns = Ns Ar address
Join only the access point with this address.
.It Cm priority Ns = Ns Ar n
A network with a larger
.Ar n
is preferred.
.It Cm key_mgmt Ns = Ns Ar list
.Cm NONE
for an open network,
.Cm WPA-PSK
for WPA and WPA2 with a passphrase,
.Cm SAE
for WPA3-Personal,
.Cm WPA-PSK SAE
for a network in WPA3's transition mode, and
.Cm WPA-EAP
for 802.1X.
The default is
.Cm WPA-PSK WPA-EAP .
.It Cm proto Ns = Ns Ar list
.Cm WPA ,
.Cm RSN
(WPA2 and WPA3), or both, the default.
.It Cm pairwise Ns = , Cm group Ns = Ns Ar list
The ciphers allowed,
.Cm CCMP
and
.Cm TKIP
among them; both by default.
.It Cm psk Ns = Ns Qq Ar passphrase
.It Cm psk Ns = Ns Ar key
The passphrase, of 8 to 63 characters, or the 64 hexadecimal digits of the
key that
.Xr wpa_passphrase 8
computes.
SAE uses the passphrase when no
.Cm sae_password
is given.
.It Cm sae_password Ns = Ns Qq Ar password
The password of WPA3-Personal.
.It Cm ieee80211w Ns = Ns Ar n
Management-frame protection for this network, as
.Cm pmf .
SAE needs 2, and the transition mode 1.
.It Cm eap Ns = Ns Ar method
.Cm PEAP ,
.Cm TTLS
or
.Cm TLS .
.It Cm identity Ns = Ns Qq Ar user
.It Cm anonymous_identity Ns = Ns Qq Ar user
.It Cm password Ns = Ns Qq Ar password
The user's name, the name sent outside the tunnel, and the password used
inside it.
.It Cm phase2 Ns = Ns Qq Ar method
The method inside the tunnel:
.Ql auth=MSCHAPV2 ,
.Ql auth=GTC
or
.Ql auth=MD5
for PEAP and TTLS, which also takes
.Ql autheap=MSCHAPV2 .
.It Cm ca_cert Ns = Ns Qq Ar file
The authorities that may sign the server's certificate.
.Ql probe://
reports the server's certificate in a
.Cm CTRL-EVENT-EAP-PEER-CERT
event with its subject and SHA-256 hash, and fails before any credential
is sent;
.Ql hash://server/sha256/ Ns Ar hash
accepts only the server whose certificate has that hash.
.It Cm domain_suffix_match Ns = Ns Qq Ar domain
Accept only a server certificate for a name in
.Ar domain .
.It Cm client_cert Ns = , Cm private_key Ns = , Cm private_key_passwd Ns = Ns Qq Ar value
The client's certificate, its key and the key's passphrase, for EAP-TLS.
.It Cm bgscan Ns = Ns Qq Cm simple : Ns Ar short : Ns Ar dbm : Ns Ar long
Scan every
.Ar short
seconds while the signal is below
.Ar dbm ,
and every
.Ar long
seconds otherwise, and move to a stronger access point of the network.
.It Cm disabled Ns =1
Leave the network out until
.Xr wpa_cli 8
enables it.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
A WPA2 network, a WPA3 network preferred to it, and a WPA2-Enterprise
network:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
ctrl_interface=/var/run/wpa_supplicant
update_config=1

network={
	ssid="home"
	psk="a long passphrase"
	bgscan="simple:30:-70:3600"
}

network={
	ssid="home6"
	key_mgmt=SAE
	sae_password="another passphrase"
	ieee80211w=2
	priority=5
}

network={
	ssid="campus"
	key_mgmt=WPA-EAP
	eap=PEAP
	identity="student"
	password="secret"
	phase2="auth=MSCHAPV2"
	ca_cert="/etc/campus-ca.pem"
}
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr wpa_cli 8 ,
.Xr wpa_passphrase 8 ,
.Xr wpa_supplicant 8
